hey guys this is vadim with max tech and  both my brother max  the other host of this channel and i  have been using the iphone 12 pro max  for over a month and we now have a good  amount of experience with it  so in this video i want to share the top  10  problems that we've noticed after using  the 12 pro max for a month  and i'll give you some very interesting  conclusions and purchasing advice  at the end of this video now before i  begin i do want to mention that for max  his biggest concern was the larger size  of the pro max  and he was actually considering buying  the regular 12 pro  instead but because of the camera  differences  he went with the max model and as it  turns out  the camera was actually quite  disappointing so before i get into those  problems let's start with problem number  one first off  one of the biggest problems is the lack  of a 120 hertz display  since so many other premium flagship  phones  already have high refresh rate displays  even mid-range phones these days  have higher than 60hz refresh rates the  oneplus 7 pro was released almost two  years ago  at a 669 dollar price tag  and it comes with a 90 hertz display  it's embarrassing that we're about to  enter into 2021  and apple doesn't at least have a 90hz  display on their 1100 flagship iphone  so that's definitely a problem but  thankfully rumors are pointing to next  year's pro models  getting 120 hertz refresh rates now  getting into problem number two  it has to do with the new square sides  while we absolutely love them because  they make the phone feel  new unique and they help with grip in  the hand  there are definitely some problems with  the new sides first off they make the  iphone 12s look very  thick despite actually being thinner  this year because of those square edges  the pro max kind of digs into your hand  while you're using it one-handed  so you can't reach as far up on the  display as with the iphone 11s  and it's also less comfortable if you're  holding it in landscape mode  since it can dig into your pinky so it  can be pretty annoying if you're holding  it like that for an extended period of  time  on top of that the new flat sides show  fingerprints  much more easily than before this is a  b-roll shot of my iphone  without cleaning it off or intentionally  adding fingerprints  it's like this all the time so i've  noticed that i spend more  time than ever before trying to keep it  clean moving on to problem number three  it really sucks that we no longer get a  charger in the box  the missing headphones i don't really  care for because i usually leave them in  the box  but as for the charging brick i was  really excited to get one  and since the current bricks from apple  use usbc  i could have actually used it for  charging other usbc devices  so it sucks that apple will no longer be  shipping out any more charging bricks  and now let's finally get into the  cameras with problem number four  something unique this year is that the  telephoto lens on the 12 pro max  finally has a longer optical zoom range  2.5 times  instead of two times on the regular pro  this was actually one of the reasons  why max chose to get the max model  instead  however there are definitely multiple  problems with it  first off to make the longer zoom  possible the aperture  was downgraded from f 2.0 to f 2.2  which basically takes in less light  because of that  the quality of zoom shots is actually  worse  on the pro max which completely ruins  the point  of the longer telephoto zoom lens on top  of that  night mode telephoto shots take longer  because it needs more time to collect  light  compared to the regular pro and taking  it even further  more zoomed in shots are harder to  stabilize  also adding to the time it takes to take  a night mode shot  i also feel like telephoto portrait  shots are less convenient  because of the extra zoom forcing you to  move back  further to get the subject in frame so  because  of all of that i found myself always  just using the regular wide camera  for portrait shots and it shouldn't be  like that  and even for daytime photos i struggle  to find an  improvement in quality between the 12  pro's maximum 10x  zoom and the 12 pro max's 12x zoom  now it's not just the telephoto lens  that's different on the pro max  apple also made a huge deal about the  sensor  on the wide camera being 47  larger than on the pro so this brings us  into problem number five apple said that  the pro max  gives you 87 better low-light photos  but when i compared them i honestly  didn't see  that big of a difference and for night  mode shots  it does help but it's not that big of a  deal  the biggest difference i noticed was  that night mode shots  take a shorter amount of time to take  the photo  which is very convenient since you don't  have to wait as long  but in terms of quality it was hard to  tell a difference  now when you're taking photos with the  wide camera during the daytime  it is extremely difficult to notice any  difference at all  on top of that the pro max gets the new  sensor shift  optical stabilization which does an  excellent job  but the 12 pro also does a great job of  stabilization  into the average person they probably  wouldn't notice the difference  taking it even further we've noticed  that the pro max is wide camera  is much worse in terms of the minimum  focusing distance  the regular pro can focus much closer to  the subject  and because of that the bokeh in the  background  actually looks bigger for macro shots  now problem number six is one that  really really annoys me and that is lens  flare  while shooting photos or videos at night  check out this video recorded on the 12  pro max  as you can see the lights are reflecting  off of the lens  itself and causing really bad flaring  this is extremely distracting when  trying to record a video of lights like  this  or maybe something like a christmas  light show an  1100 iphone shouldn't be having  this big of a problem now this also  happens for photos  like this one of my son in front of the  fireplace  there is a really distracting flare from  the fire that's positioned  right in front of him and it kind of  ruins the photo  this is actually a much bigger issue on  the 12 pro max specifically  because the camera lenses are much  larger and the lens glass itself  sticks out further than the exterior  metal rings  which causes light to reflect off of  them  so in this comparison you can see how  the pro-max  is worse than the other models so it's  definitely been causing problems  over the past month moving on to problem  number seven it has to do  with max safe and max safe accessories  when we first got the max safe wallet  and tested it out on the iphone 12 pro  it worked pretty well and we didn't  really notice much issues with it being  bumped out of place  or falling off when putting it into your  pocket however  with the 12 pro max the wallet is  noticeably worse  and i think it's because there is extra  dead space on the back of the iphone  so there's more room for it to move  around and get knocked out of place  we actually confirmed that theory by  using the wallet with the iphone 12 mini  where the edges of the wallet are  perfectly flush with the sides of the  mini  and because of that it's extremely hard  to accidentally bump the wallet out of  place  because your hand is supporting it from  the other side  so the wallet experience is by far the  worst  on the pro max which is very  disappointing now the magsafe problems  don't end there  apple's new mac save charger is problem  number eight  for forty dollars it's simply not worth  it at  all yes it's convenient that it attaches  magnetically  but the charging speed is unbearably  slow  max made a crazy detail charging  comparison video  and he found that even with the new 20  watt usbc charging brick  max safe was only 15 minutes faster  than the old 5 watt charging brick when  charging from zero to 100 percent  yes it was quite a bit faster in the  beginning of the test  but when you hear 15 watt max say fast  charging  you'd expect it to be just a little bit  slower than the 20 watt cable charging  but that ended up finishing the test a  full hour sooner  than maxsafe so in my personal opinion  the magsafe charger is a problem because  it charges  way slower than apple is leading people  to believe now for mistake number nine  it has to do with overheating the new  iphone 12s come with the latest  a14 bionic chip which is made using  tsmc's  brand new 5 nanometer technology which  is super efficient  however max was doing some call of duty  mobile gaming  in a very bright barber shop so the  display brightness automatically  brightened up and he noticed that after  just 10 minutes  the display dimmed because of  overheating  this is an issue because the five  nanometer chip is supposed to be more  efficient  and it's supposed to run more cool so we  thought that we'd no longer have these  overheating issues ever again  but that's not the case other phone  manufacturers like samsung have been  implementing cooling solutions  like a built-in vapor chamber to reduce  overheating problems but apple doesn't  seem to care  so it's a bit annoying when you have to  deal with these issues  on such an expensive flagship phone and  finally  let's get into problem number 10. the  iphone 12 pro max  is still using the lightning port and  we're honestly getting a bit sick of it  while every other device on the market  is moving over to the usb-c  port apple refuses to switch if the  iphone had a usb-c  port everything from file transfers to  charging  would be much more convenient i'd love  to be able to grab my macbook charging  cable  and quickly charge up my iphone but i  can't  because it uses lightning and now even  the ipad air 4  uses usbc but not the iphone  which is starting to get very annoying  because we now know  just how much better usbc is than  lightning  in basically every way so with all of  those 10 problems out of the way  my final conclusion or advice is that if  you are thinking about going for the 12  pro max  model maybe for the extra camera  improvements  it's really not worth it in reality the  camera differences weren't that big  so if you were thinking about getting  the regular 6.1 inch 12 pro model  go for it so there you guys have it that  was our top 10 problems with the iphone  12 pro max after a full month of use  so if you agree or disagree with any of  those  please comment your thoughts down below  and click the circle above to subscribe  for our full iphone 12 pro max review  that's coming very soon  thank you guys for watching and we'll  see you in the next video
 

